        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "An order of preventive detention may be made with or without prosecution and in anticipation or after discharge or even acquittal."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "61e9b2aaf2ce457481e165ea83ca838a_32",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The pendency of prosecution is no bar to an order of preventive detention."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7bc584887cfe46339ad6eae673eb4288_33",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "An order of preventive detention is also not a bar to prosecution."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "8d0e7516f39e43b2b29e06cfe73bfc5a_34",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "33. Article 14 is inapplicable because preventive detention and prosecution are not synonymous."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7debf00acf3e4fb1882aec5abedd5fdc_35",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The purposes are different."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2e5d550de78e49f3916158a860826385_36",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The authorities are different."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6c95c359f0a94fd2ac5e0af5cce8344e_37",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The nature of proceedings is different."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "f821757131774e049e585992744a21a3_38",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In a prosecution an accused is sought to be punished for a past act."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "924ce3bf502940a994f3a74ff153b51c_39",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In preventive detention, the past act is merely the material for inference about the future course of probable conduct on the part of the detenu.\""
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "462a91b64fa247c588edc94d0937b2f1_40",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nFrom the bare perusal of the aforesaid position of law laid down by the Apex court it is manifest that a detenue can be detained notwithstanding his detention or involvement in a criminal case, as the power of preventive detention is preca"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "38e25dab814c42c39ee19a191a135c37_41",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Thus, in view of the aforesaid legal position, the aforesaid ground urged by counsel for the petitioner cannot be accepted and is accordingly rejected."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "61bd7a5246d24e8baa93b28935f0a399_42",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n6. Insofar as the next ground urged by counsel for the petitioner that the grounds of detention are vague non-specific and irrelevant, a reference to the grounds of detention annexed with the petition becomes imperative."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "246caca8201447c78d5d49484f1e81bf_43",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In para 2 and 3 of the grounds of detention it is stated by the detaining authority while referring to the detenue that at a young you age having met with various separatists and other fringe elements under whose influence you developed rad"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "793f8ceb035448c3831b6b64e92272a9_44",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "In the grounds of detention after para 4 it is stated that you came to be apprehended on 15.03.2023 under section 107, CrPC read with 151 CrPC as it was made to believe that you may indulge in breach of peace and tranquility in the area and"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b9f8d1d70891411f9f7074af74a3acb7_45",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The detaining authority appears to have taken into consideration the past activities of the detenue as also his detention thereof under the provisions of the Code of Criminal Procedure and consequent to his release has not detailed out spec"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7d525022b91b4674b53a73a7b07b73ab_46",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Non-furnishing of the said specific details to the detenue in the grounds of detention has been held to be vague vitiating the order of detention."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2ddfaf5f3fe24437baed228754247984_47",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reliance in this regard is placed on the judgment of the Apex court passed in case titled as \"Mohammed Yousuf Rather Vs.\nState of Jammu and Kashmir"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ee07167f7ba1486e95f7c8285a226718_48",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\" reported in 1979 (4) SCCC 370 wherein at para 8 and 13 it has been held as under: -\n8."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "23b40a5a350549fc9233d59708171429_49",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is obvious therefore that the above grounds of detention are vague."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "6296d23fb12749d6966047c154ec9dfd_50",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nThis Court has disapproved of vagueness in the grounds of detention because that impinges on the fundamental right of the detenu under Article 22(5) of the Constitution to make a representation against the order of detention when the groun"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "988e2b417fcd459c819f748c41f3ef3a_51",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The purpose of the requirement is to afford him the earliest opportunity of seeking redress against the order of detention."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "b71e6ddddd214198bf7f51d7150f5efc_52",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "But as is obvious, that opportunity cannot be said to be afforded when it is established that a ground of detention is so vague that he cannot possibly Aqib Ahmad Shergojri Aged 28 vs ) Union Territory Of J&K on 4 June, 2024 Indian Kanoon -"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "1d43d84ff91d420199e605000c8e2935_53",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference in this connection may be made to this Court's decision in State of Bombay v. Atma Ram Sridhar Vaidya (1951 SCR 167) where the guarantee of article 22(5)\nhas been characterised as an elementary right of a citizen in a free democra"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "9642521086b1474cb14c2a3cc71021ca_54",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "So as the aforesaid grounds of detention are vague, the petitioner is entitled to an order of release for that reason alone."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "2ccc3eed5bc043dea1fb68aba0e33162_55",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is true that, as has been held in Naresh Chandra Ganguli's case, (supra) \"vagueness\" is a relative term, and varies according to the circumstances of each case,\nbut if the statement of facts contains any ground of detention which is such"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "021961adf6cb4276a95064edd21deb13_56",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference in this connection may also be made to the decisions in Tarapada De and others v. The State of West Bengal, (1951 SCR 212) Dr. Ram Krishan Bhardwaj v. State of Delhi and other (1953 SCR 708), Shibban Lal Saxena v. State of Uttar P"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "73fb8b40072a44a18450d2b2c0ab335c_57",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It is well settled that a ground is said to be irrelevant when it has no connection with the satisfaction of the authority making the order of detention under the appropriate law."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "e794e85760ee4cc7aff9a0ccbb232139_58",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It nevertheless appears that the aforesaid irrelevant grounds were taken into consideration for making the impugned order, and that is quite sufficient to vitiate it."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "73a18c2cb0bc442bb98611a4c48cf80c_59",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Reference in this connection may be made to the decisions in Keshav Talpade v. The King Emperor, 1943 FCR 49, Tarapada De and others v. State of West Bengal (supra), Shibban Lal Saxena v. State of Uttar Pradesh and others (supra), Pushkar M"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "5d325fb7c8d547d0b7baef7b298493ae_60",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "It has been held there that even if one of the grounds of detention is irrelevant, that is sufficient to vitate the order."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "321d3b54188546f5b99ff189cb3ba7df_61",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "The reason is that it is not possible to assess in what manner and to what extent that irrelevant ground operated on the mind of the appropriate authority and contributed to provide the satisfaction that it was necessary to detain the petit"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "fe0f81b7b1f3481ca934b7cb7a8348b5_62",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\nOn this ground thus, the impugned order cannot said to be legally sustainable."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "41fe804dea92431eb8eb7ec14cd46d4e_63",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "\n7. Insofar as the 3rd ground pressed by counsel for the petition qua non consideration of the representation submitted by the petitioner is concerned, perusal of the record produced by counsel for the respondents tend to show that represen"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "979b924094b24198a2975c56c40a0540_64",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Detention record further reveals that a copy of representation submitted by the petitioner had been forwarded to the advisory board as well on 20.04.2023 which also considered the same inasmuch as heard the detenue in person on 10.05.2023 a"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "c4da0bcecb8640f4be0cd073f3f76c7a_65",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "PRE_RELIED"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "8. It is settled position of law laid down by the Apex court in a series of judgments including in case titled as \"V. Shantha Vs. State of Telengana\" reported in 2017 (14) SCC 577 that an order of preventive detention though based on the su"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "7532ee65c87d49c6bcadd6ac3fe9ecc9_66",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Having regard to what has been observed, considered and analyzed above, in particular that the ground of detention drawn and framed by the detaining authority are vague, irrelevant and insignificant having resulted into deprivation of the p"
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "db32bfa07c9d438086e36e61a7db5ef1_67",
        "summary_section": "ANALYSIS",
        "labels": [
          "RATIO"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:ANALYSIS"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [],
        "text_preview": "Under these circumstances the impugned order cannot be said to be legally sustainable."
      },
      {
        "annotation_id": "ad66d2237650476d90d1be80605c4955_68",
        "summary_section": "decision",
        "labels": [
          "RPC"
        ],
        "reasons": [
          "forbidden_section:decision",
          "forbidden_labels:RPC",
          "suspicious_label:rpc",
          "explicit_leakage_phrase"
        ],
        "matched_phrases": [
          {
